User request: Add Xpress AI workflow automation to xai-xpressai for workloads running inside the Platform, using injected job/service environment variables. Leave xai-tasks unchanged. Companion backend: XpressAI/platform PR 577; architectural contract is Platform ADR-079.

Change: Seven native Xircuits components list agents/procedures, create tasks, start saved procedures, read/wait for task state, and answer settled waiting tasks. The client requires Platform URL, canonical project ID, namespace, and project workload token, and never sends Relay credentials, inference keys, or an agent identity claim. Jobs derive replay keys from job/node IDs; services and loops use explicit business keys. HTTP calls are bounded, redirects and implicit write retries are disabled, and status outputs distinguish Waiting, Failed and Done.

Examples and rollout: Added a compiled scheduled approval workflow, saved procedure example, full port/auth/retry instructions, and CI. Deploy Platform PR 577 before updating this library. These components use ordinary agent execution; they do not implement READY and do not certify a live enterprise approval demo.

Validation: 34 pytest cases passed with the actual Xircuits 1.19.2 component base and compiler, local HTTP fixtures, and execution of the saved .xircuits graph. Cases cover environment credential isolation, task/status port connections, shared procedure inputs, waiting/resume state fences, timeout behavior, redirect refusal, HTTP errors, malformed responses, and deterministic per-job/node keys. Existing four Relay authorization regressions also pass as part of that total. Backend tests independently exercise actual PostgreSQL migrations and concurrent task creation/approval responses. No live agent, Relay, legacy application, or production task/schedule was invoked.
